  "question": {
    "text": "A spherical iron ball $10 \\mathrm{~cm}$ in radius is coated with a layer of ice of uniform thickness than melts at a rate of $50 \\mathrm{~cm}^3 / \\mathrm{min}$. When the thickness of ice is $5 \\mathrm{~cm}$, then the rate at which the thickness of ice decreases, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "66FUk",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{36 \\pi} \\mathrm{cm} / \\mathrm{min}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "agC7w",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{18 \\pi} \\mathrm{cm} / \\mathrm{min}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "kqYUk",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{54 \\pi} \\mathrm{cm} / \\mathrm{min}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "V2YI4",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{5}{6 \\pi} \\mathrm{cm} / \\min$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{d v}{d t}=50 \\\\\n& 4 \\pi r^2 \\frac{d r}{d t}=50 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{d r}{d t}=\\frac{50}{4 \\pi(15)^2} \\quad \\text { where } r=15 \\\\\n& =\\frac{1}{16 \\pi}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
